{"name":"Bogotá","slug":"bogota","region":"Latin America","lat":4.71,"lon":-74.07,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Bogotá has warmed by about 0.2 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.5 °C in all, with the coldest days warming fastest, so cold extremes are becoming rarer. There is a strong, well-established El Niño effect on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer, and El Niño accounts for about 40% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 2 times a normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 48 years of the long-term trend. Without El Niño, a Dec–Feb this warm would come about once every 39 years. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 1.2 °C, against 0.7 °C for the coldest days. Dec–Feb rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a drier season with fewer rainy days and less intense heavy-rain days, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a less humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is very likely (more than 95% chance), about 1.4 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a drier-than-normal season is likely (about 90% chance), and a less humid season than normal is likely (about 65% chance). This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":13.8187,"trend_per_decade":0.2031,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.5229,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.4466,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.4093,"intrinsic_sd":0.5029,"effect_this_season":0.9825,"effect_ratio":1.9538,"size":"Dominant","size_typical_el_nino":"Dominant","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":39.0,"expected_anomaly_2027":1.3811,"p_below":0.0018,"p_near":0.0055,"p_above":0.9927,"forecast_words":"Very likely (>95%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":48.383,"values":[11.531,12.034,12.324,11.813,12.288,11.294,11.747,14.759,12.958,12.539,13.405,13.736,13.512,13.795,13.195,13.703,13.253,13.407,13.653,14.203,13.278,13.038,14.117,12.426,13.192,12.75,13.903,13.945,12.912,13.092,14.023,13.281,14.159,12.29,13.278,12.721,13.748,13.664,12.816,13.582,13.882,13.824,13.843,12.979,13.819,13.123,13.247,14.804,13.641,13.447,13.236,14.303,14.243,13.975,14.816,13.689,14.165,13.478,13.604,14.889,13.258,13.416,13.741,13.981,13.666,14.966,13.585,13.309,13.807,13.826,13.768,13.934,12.995,14.061,13.664],"forecast_mean":15.1997,"forecast_sd":0.5499,"fit":{"a2027":14.2173,"b":0.4466,"c":0.0203,"tercile_low":13.5976,"tercile_high":13.8557},"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.2281,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.3255,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":0.7162,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.2047,"trend_p"