 normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 53 years of the long-term trend. Without El Niño, a Mar–May this warm would come less than once a century. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 1.2 °C, against 0.7 °C for the coldest days. Mar–May rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a drier season with fewer rainy days, and this year's shift is substantial. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a less humid Mar–May, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. For Mar–May 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is very likely (more than 95% chance), about 1.4 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a less humid season than normal is likely (about 70% chance). This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":13.7816,"trend_per_decade":0.1855,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.391,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.4431,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.503,"intrinsic_sd":0.4128,"effect_this_season":0.9748,"effect_ratio":2.3614,"size":"Dominant","size_typical_el_nino":"Dominant","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":">100","expected_anomaly_2027":1.3934,"p_below":0.0001,"p_near":0.0037,"p_above":0.9962,"forecast_words":"Very likely (>95%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":52.5597,"values":[12.029,12.482,12.7,12.101,11.788,11.841,12.384,14.682,13.389,12.864,13.564,13.12,13.714,13.562,13.291,13.834,13.075,13.246,14.235,14.062,12.721,13.142,14.33,12.779,12.988,12.696,13.579,13.148,13.249,14.052,13.971,13.342,14.304,13.311,13.327,12.875,13.911,13.617,12.708,13.678,13.722,14.308,13.522,13.121,13.55,12.979,13.438,14.57,12.832,13.202,13.672,13.697,13.659,13.952,14.614,13.382,13.955,13.4